 # tidy-tasks
 
+Document version: 1.1 (2026-10-26)
+
 The task list behind Tidy Tasks, a small to-do app for households and small teams. People add tasks with
 a title, a priority and a few tags, tick them off when they are done, and look at what is left, most
 urgent first. This package holds the list itself, in TypeScript; the app's screens use its public API
@@ -12,3 +14,9 @@ Run its tests with `npm test`.
 Each task returned by `add` has a list-unique string `id`. IDs remain unchanged when a task is
 renamed. Use `get(id)` to look up a task by ID; `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`,
 `untag`, and `remove` also accept either a task title or its ID.
+
+## Task timestamps
+
+Every returned task has ISO-8601 `createdAt` and `updatedAt` date-time strings. Both are set when the
+task is added. `updatedAt` changes whenever completing, reopening, renaming, tagging, or untagging
+causes an effective change to that task.
